---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

// NOTE FOR ADVRT: this notice describes exactly what this website does, which
// is accurate as built. The items in [SQUARE BRACKETS] are facts only you can
// supply (company number, ICO registration, retention periods, and the name of
// the CRM the webhook forwards to). Have it checked before the domain goes live.
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy notice · ADVRT"
  description="How ADVRT collects, uses and protects personal data submitted through this website."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy notice"
  updated="6 November 2026"
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    ADVRT (“we”, “us”) is the data controller for personal data submitted through this website.
    We are a marketing agency working with firms in the built environment.
  </p>
  <address>
    {site.address.line1}, {site.address.line2}<br />
    {site.address.city} {site.address.postcode}<br />
    United Kingdom
  </address>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> ·
    Telephone <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    Company registration number [COMPANY NUMBER]. ICO registration reference [ICO REFERENCE].
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    We only collect what you type into one of the two forms on this site. We do not use advertising
    cookies, third-party analytics or tracking pixels on this website, and nothing on it profiles you.
  </p>

  <h3>The project brief</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, firm, email address and telephone number</li>
    <li>The areas you cover and any notes you add</li>
    <li>Your answers about your sector, the work you want, your current lead sources, your website, your budget range and your timescale</li>
    <li>Your preferred day and time for a discovery call, if you pick one</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>The contact form</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your name, company, email address and telephone number</li>
    <li>The topic you select and the message you write</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Collected automatically</h3>
  <p>
    When a form is submitted, our hosting provider records the page it came from, the referring page,
    and your browser's user agent string alongside the submission. Our host also keeps standard
    server logs, which include IP addresses, for security and abuse prevention.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To reply to your enquiry and prepare a plan or quote.</strong> Our lawful basis is
      legitimate interests: you contacted us asking for exactly this, and responding is what you expect.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To arrange and hold a discovery call</strong> where you have asked for one. Lawful basis:
      legitimate interests, and steps towards a contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To keep a record of enquiries and prevent abuse of the forms.</strong> Lawful basis:
      legitimate interests.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not add you to a marketing list from a website enquiry, and we do not send marketing email
    unless you separately ask us to.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Form submissions are passed to the systems we use to run the business. These act as our
    processors, handle the data on our instructions only, and do not use it for their own purposes.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Netlify</strong> — hosts this website and runs the function that receives your submission.</li>
    <li><strong>[CRM NAME]</strong> — our customer relationship system, where enquiries are stored and worked.</li>
    <li><strong>[EMAIL / MESSAGING PROVIDER]</strong> — used to acknowledge your enquiry and to send call confirmations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal data, and we do not share your enquiry with other firms. An enquiry you
    send us goes to us alone.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a provider processes data outside the UK, that transfer is covered by the UK's adequacy
    regulations or by an International Data Transfer Agreement or Addendum.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries that do not become clients:</strong> [RETENTION PERIOD, e.g. 24 months] from your last contact with us, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Client records:</strong> for the duration of our work together and [RETENTION PERIOD] afterwards, to meet our legal and accounting obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> as long as our host retains them, which is a short rolling window.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Give you a copy of the personal data we hold about you</li>
    <li>Correct it if it is wrong, or complete it if it is incomplete</li>
    <li>Delete it, where we have no overriding reason to keep it</li>
    <li>Restrict or object to how we use it, including objecting to our legitimate interests</li>
    <li>Transfer it to you or another provider in a portable format</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond within one month.
    There is no charge.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data you can complain to the Information
    Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, or by
    calling 0303 123 1113. We would rather you raised it with us first so we can put it right.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and uses no browser storage. There is no cookie banner because
    there is nothing to consent to. If we add analytics later, this notice will be updated and
    consent will be requested before anything non-essential is set.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we use personal data we will update this page and the date at the top of it.
  </p>
</Legal>
